description:
FILED s521b (Opus, 2026-10-18).  Pre-existing; newly REACHED: perl-tests/readline.t's last SKIP block calls PerlIO::get_layers
before its four assertions, and until #3326 (s521b) the missing sub aborted the block.  Rows 33-34 now pass; 35-36 fail on this:

    use IO::Handle;
    open my $fh, ">", "/tmp/x" or die;
    my $l = <$fh>;
    print "read=", (defined $l ? 1 : 0), " error=", ($fh->error ? 1 : 0), " close=", (close($fh) ? 1 : 0), "\n";
    perl 5.40.3: read=0 error=1 close=0        PCL: read=0 error=0 close=1

The handle error flag already exists for a failed WRITE (DECIDED: perl_destruct's STDOUT rule -- a failed write sets the handle
error flag, close then false); a failed READ (EBADF on a write-only handle) must set the same flag.  Rows blessed in
baselines/fail-baseline.tsv with this cause (s521b).
